# rules: todo-comments
# fixture: generic/todo-comments.txt
#
# Every TODO, FIXME, HACK, XXX and BUG left in a comment, in any language:
# the notes a codebase keeps about what it knows is unfinished. The marker and
# what follows it are the message, so a list of these reads as a backlog.
#
# It is a regex over text rather than a pattern, because a comment is not
# syntax any grammar gives a shape to, and the rule should not care which
# language it is reading. The marker has to follow a comment opener - `//`,
# `#`, `/*`, `*`, `--` or `;` - so an identifier called todoList is not one.

scan_regex("*"; "(?m)(?://|#|/\\*|^\\s*\\*|--|;)\\s*(?P<NOTE>(?:TODO|FIXME|HACK|XXX|BUG)\\b.*?)\\s*(?:\\*/)?$")
| finding("todo-comments"; "$NOTE")
| report
